(3117632, 433680, 44099, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all the comments guys. This contest was a surprisingly low scorer...nonetheless, even with a 5.6, I was able to sneak into top 50, which is good enough for me :)</td>', 'Thanks for all the comments guys. This contest was a surprisingly low scorer...nonetheless, even with a 5.6, I was able to sneak into top 50, which is good enough for me :)', '2006-12-14 14:49:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(3117698, 435181, 66384, '<td valign="top">Your photo is well composed and very moving. I saw too much of this during the years I lived and worked in NYC. I understand the people who are just walking by. It''s terrible that we become so hardened to this sort of suffering. This image says a lot.</td>', 'Your photo is well composed and very moving. I saw too much of this during the years I lived and worked in NYC. I understand the people who are just walking by. It''s terrible that we become so hardened to this sort of suffering. This image says a lot.', '2006-12-14 15:28:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(3118097, 435136, 55642, '<td valign="top">I think you did get dinged for the lack of understanding of what seppuku is, but your biggest hit actually comes from the photo''s reliance on the title to meet the challenge. That makes it a shoehorn in many eyes. It''s also a very dark photo, so an uncalibrated monitor could make it very very very dark (like the monitor I''m on now at work, which sucks a whole lot). Dark photos <i>very rarely</i> do well on DPC for this reason. I gave this a 5, because it''s a really nice photo, but even knowing what seppuku is without looking it up I really don''t see how the title is connected to the photo. The pose doesn''t suggest seppuku to me at all. It might have if there was a samurai sword involved, or a more upright, dignified pose suggesting the honor of the ritual. On my scale, an outstanding photo that I find DNMC doesn''t usually score higher than a 4. I gave this an extra point because it''s technically solid and <i>might</i> have had a stronger connection to death with a different title, perhaps something more connected to the grief over the death of a loved one, which I can see as a decent interpretation for this picture.</td>', 'I think you did get dinged for the lack of understanding of what seppuku is, but your biggest hit actually comes from the photo''s reliance on the title to meet the challenge. That makes it a shoehorn in many eyes. It''s also a very dark photo, so an uncalibrated monitor could make it very very very dark (like the monitor I''m on now at work, which sucks a whole lot). Dark photos very rarely do well on DPC for this reason. I gave this a 5, because it''s a really nice photo, but even knowing what seppuku is without looking it up I really don''t see how the title is connected to the photo. The pose doesn''t suggest seppuku to me at all. It might have if there was a samurai sword involved, or a more upright, dignified pose suggesting the honor of the ritual. On my scale, an outstanding photo that I find DNMC doesn''t usually score higher than a 4. I gave this an extra point because it''s technically solid and might have had a stronger connection to death with a different title, perhaps something more connected to the grief over the death of a loved one, which I can see as a decent interpretation for this picture.', '2006-12-14 18:23:35.000000', NULL, 0),
